    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T07:19:52Z",
    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main 1d3d93541: a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_through_the_disk_reader passes without a production change. It calls default_machine_checked in one isolated process with disk files missing, then {}, then the good shipped file. It gets Err, Err, Ok and keeps the good parsed machine after a later broken file.\n\nCommit 84c5a8b09 in PR #2320 removed the text cache from default_mch_text. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe requested regression coverage is still absent upstream. This result confirms the behavior only. I stopped because the assigned Step 5 explicitly requires the new test to fail on unchanged code and says to stop if it passes. No mutation, gate, production change, commit, push, or PR followed.\n\nClaim released. The uncommitted test remains in .claude/worktrees/issue-2324 on issue/2324-default-machine-disk-pin. A patch and the passing output are saved outside the repository at /private/tmp/2324-disk-pin.patch and /private/tmp/2324-pin.log.\n",
